# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git tracks every file in this folder unless a rule below matches it.
# A line starting with ! is an EXCEPTION -- it un-ignores something.
#
# The key idea: some "IDE files" are personal (yours alone) and some are
# project files (everyone's). We ignore the personal ones and COMMIT the
# project ones. That is what lets one clone open in Eclipse, VS Code, and
# Cursor with nobody reconfiguring anything.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Compiled output: generated from source, never committed -----------------
bin/
out/
target/
build/
*.class

# --- Secrets and local environment -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.keystore

# --- Eclipse: personal workspace state ---------------------------------------
# NOTE: .project and .classpath are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the
# shared project definition and MUST be committed.
.metadata/
.recommenders/
.apt_generated/
.factorypath
.externalToolBuilders/
tmp/
.settings/*
!.settings/org.eclipse.jdt.core.prefs
!.settings/org.eclipse.core.resources.prefs

# --- VS Code / Cursor: ignore personal state, keep shared config -------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
*.code-workspace

# --- IntelliJ / NetBeans ------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
nbproject/private/
nbbuild/
nbdist/

# --- Operating-system clutter -------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Logs and JVM crash reports ----------------------------------------------
*.log
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
